Z||000003||mope||02-04-2001||10:12 PM||||can anyone talk me thru what is supposed to be there? there isnt much for me to work with..all i saw was a cable from lever to left rear then say a piece just hanging not connected to anything in the back that looked like it went ftom the left  to the rite. now that im thinking that doesnt seem right..does the one from the front split then go to left and right?<P>thanks<P>m0pe||||reg||5
Z||000004||2birds||02-04-2001||10:16 PM||||My entire cable assembly was replaced under the recall that replaced the rear calipers.  Recall # 86-C-16, or something like that.  If it's been it done already, I think you're SOL as far as getting it done for free.  <BR>Run the VIN at the dealer to see if it's been done, or check the rear caliper pistons.  The ones that don't have the vent valves in the center of the rear caliper pistons are the post-recall design.  <BR>Since you have a manual tranny, it should have been done, but Pontiac isn't very good about tracking the owners down, IMHO.  <p>[This message has been edited by 2birds (edited 02-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||mope||02-04-2001||11:08 PM||||what do these vent valves look like?||||reg||1
Z||000006||2birds||02-05-2001||06:57 AM||||They are about 1/2" across, made of soft plastic, and are in the center of the pad side of the rear caliper piston.  The new style pistons have no holes in the pad side face.  ||||reg||1
